// SHORTCUTS domain (RFC-0113 §7, TASK-0346 P3) — the keyboard-shortcuts window that
// `Allgemeine Verwaltung › Eingabe › Tastaturkurzbefehle` opens over the settings window.
// Every row is REGISTRY truth from `svc.shortcuts.list(category, locale)`: the chords come from
// the one table inputd and the keymap match keys against, named for the device's language —
// this window holds no chord of its own. Rebinding is a later phase: its controls are drawn,
// disabled.

Store ShortcutsStore {
    // The window is open.
    scOpen: Bool = false,
    // The category on screen: windows | screenshots | text | input.
    scCategory: Str = "windows",
    // Its rows (`ShortcutRow { id, keys, alt, active }`); [] until listed.
    shortcuts: List<ShortcutRow> = [],
    // Non-zero effect error code when the list failed.
    scError: Int = 0,
}

Event ShortcutsEvent {
    ScOpen,
    ScClose,
    ScPick(Str),
    ScListed(List<ShortcutRow>),
    ScFailed(Int),
}

reduce ShortcutsEvent {
    ScOpen => {
        state.scOpen = true;
        state.scCategory = "windows";
    },
    ScClose => state.scOpen = false,
    ScPick(id) => state.scCategory = id,
    ScListed(rows) => {
        state.shortcuts = rows;
        state.scError = 0;
    },
    ScFailed(code) => state.scError = code,
}

// The window opens on its first category.
@effect on ScOpen {
    match svc.shortcuts.list("windows", device.locale) {
        Ok(rows) => dispatch(ScListed(rows)),
        Err(e) => dispatch(ScFailed(e)),
    }
}

@effect on ScPick(id) {
    match svc.shortcuts.list(id, device.locale) {
        Ok(rows) => dispatch(ScListed(rows)),
        Err(e) => dispatch(ScFailed(e)),
    }
}
